# Coach speech (Arabic): the rules lesson (level 0, src/coach/lesson.cpp).
# Same keys and variants as assets/coach/speech/en/lesson.lang.
#
# Placeholders: {your} / {my} = a piece of the player / of the coach ("رخّك", "حصاني": every piece
# is masculine, so "it" is always ـه / هو); {sq}, {sq2}, {to}, {esc} = squares; {move} = a move.
# {@}, {@2}, {@3} are invisible marks placed right before the word the coach points at.
# Literal Latin letters (files a-h, the knight's L) are dropped by the voice: those lines have a
# ".spoken" version with the Arabic letter names of the opening texts (أيه، إي، إتش، إل).
# "ملِك" carries a kasra in the possessives (ملِكي، ملِكك) and "رخّ" a shadda (رخّي، رخّك), as in
# common.lang, so that neither the reader nor the voice mistakes them for other words.

